                        "entry_id": "71351bd3-77a6-3b14-8711-38c0a259515c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In the manner of fingers from a hand; spreading out in several narrow parts."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "89a7874f-cd7c-4c1e-818e-4503dd255875",
                                "sense_id": "045f3a06-3888-3144-b396-606f0e5360b9",
                                "text": "In this way alone too, it seems to me, can one gain a clear and consistent idea of the valley itself as an organic whole, with the various lateral glens which open out fingerwise on every side of it as its component members."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "601d7459-9590-445d-96fa-115e1e21644f",
                                "sense_id": "045f3a06-3888-3144-b396-606f0e5360b9",
                                "text": "The valleys make natural and not ill-graded highways from the prairie to the Wisconsin River, while the ranges of bluffs separating them appear like promontories running out fingerwise from the main plateau[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
